      "summary": ": Rāhina/Monday The weekend's above forecasted snowfall has put us in good shape, fattening up the snowpack and moving us forwards! South Ridge is fully groomed for 1st time this season. We have a nice offering of groomed trails across both basins today, which will start firm and soften as day progresses. The dastardly cloud cap that came with the snow put some moisture into the snow, and overnight that has firmed up with a bit of a crust off-trail. That should break down with some tracks and could develop into good skiing/riding in the upper Saddle as day progresses. The cloud is clearing and the day is set to bring more susnhine. Bit of a SW breeze up in Saddle, but that is forecast to ease. So a day that will improve as it goes on in both weather and snow conditions. Skite will open at 1100.",
